# std/log — one of the history tools (std/git-history holds the source they share).
# The help is a HERE-STRING so it lives in this expression, which is stripped
# from the tree the build sees: editing the docs re-keys this tool's ArgTree and
# nothing it builds from.
HELP=<<END
Show a source tree's first-parent commit history newest-first: one line per commit with its short hash, date, author and subject. Optionally start from a given revision and/or restrict to commits that changed a path. Reads git history the tree alone can't show.
@param source-tree Path of the source tree (a code reference in the conversation), such as feature/01-change.
@param [rev] Where to start (default HEAD, the source tree's own commit). A commit hash, or HEAD with ~N or ^ ancestry.
@param [path] Only show commits that changed this source-tree-relative path.
@param [count] Maximum number of commits to show (default 20).
@in
END
IMAGE=run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --src:@=DEEP-DEPS/git-history --dep0:@=DEEP-DEPS/conversation-protocol --dep1:@=DEEP-DEPS/git-locator --output-runner:@=DEEP-DEPS/git-runner
curry --base=$IMAGE --op=log --help=$HELP
